    Deferred Revenues: Revenues that are received but not yet earned. For instance, if a customer pays upfront for a year of service, the amount is recognized gradually over the year.

    Reconciliation: The process of ensuring two sets of records (usually the balances of two accounts) match. In Odoo, bank statement reconciliation is a common activity where you match bank statement lines with your accounting entries.

    Journal Entries: The logging of transactions into accounting records. Every transaction has a journal entry.

